# Clean-CPS re-entry addrs: coroutine continuation / branch-target PCs that
# are NOT function entries (no fnmap row) but must route to a clean body so a
# yielded CD/IRQ coroutine resumes inside clean C. Multiple addrs may name the
# same symbol; clean_try_dispatch hands the fn cpu->pc == the dispatched addr
# so the body's pc-switch picks the right continuation block.
#
# cd_irq_init_seq (guest 0x8019A87C) — CD IRQ/init sequencing coroutine.
# Entry + its 7 CPS continuation/branch-target blocks all re-enter the same
# clean body; 0x8019A8DC is the NEXT function (stays generated).
